			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829009">
									

<p>Alright, I can go with that emotion. But how are you going to portray that through the Foundation's view? Remember, even if the Foundation is powerful, it is still mortal, and I'm afraid it can't last as long until humanity's end unless some catastrophe happens. And that catastrophe is what's needed here: yes, you have all this conceptual stuff but try zooming in to the smaller picture, are you going to tell the story of someone interacting with the painter? And how are you going to tell this story through the SCP format, especially if the catastrophe is going to happen in the far future? How will you make readers care about the painter enough to feel pity for him? Is there some kind of backstory or traits that the painter has that we can get attached to?</p>

