														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829002">
									

<p>Hey again! I see you've responded to my crit!<br />
I'll give you my thoughts on both the options you've presented:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Option&nbsp;1&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This just seems like a random ability tacked onto an (in my opinion) uninteresting concept in an effort to make it appear more interesting. Allow me to reiterate that making an SCP more dangerous <em>does not</em>, I repeat <em><strong>does not</strong></em> make it more interesting. This only serves to break the theme of the object completely. I'd strongly recommend not using this option, as a 'cloud of deadly radiation' has nothing to do with Midas or gold.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Option&nbsp;2&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This option is slightly better than the previous, but still not great. All it does is reanimate people and turn them into hostile, golden killing machines. It's boring and cliche. It also doesn't match with the myth of Midas, which is what you're basing your concept off of. Unless this goes under some heavy reworking, this option won't work either.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Anyway, that's it for this recrit. Hope this helps!
							</div>

								
					
